# basePath Chapter1
:: FirstContractOpenCh1
@trigger    OnContractSelectOpen
@cutscene
@once



//changed this from employee to trainee while he still owns his ship.

{@PAL}		As a trainee, you'll learn to operate four systems...
{@PAL}		...all recently upgraded with Frontier Robotics automation systems...
{@PAL}		...aboard this obsolete ship.
{@Player}   Hey! She's got plenty of life left in her!
{@Player}   ...I miss my old crew already.

{@PAL}      The first “contract” is your orientation. 
//Check - did I do this right? highlight should be arrow not button highlight
//$call   HighlightElement(overarching:costs-section, false, 25, true)
$call   PointElement(overarching:costs-section)
{@PAL}      This is how long the contract should take.
$call   ReleaseAllHighlights()
//ChECK:  highlight should be arrow not button highlight
//$call   HighlightElement(overarching:profit-section, false, 25, true)
$call   PointElement(overarching:profit-section)
{@PAL}      ...and this is what you'll be paid.
$call   ReleaseAllHighlights()

{@PAL}      You can chip away at that huge debt! 
$call   HighlightElement(overarching:select-contract-btn)

//{@Player}   P.A.L., I've been doing business with my team for years. 
//{@PAL}      As the Personal Automation Liaison and I'm WAY more useful than human assistants.


//EDIT - KACY 
// Added line for PAL for better flow and to reinforce debt being centeral issue player has to tackle. 

$call   UnlockWikiPage("Basic Conductor")
$call   UnlockWikiPage("Basic Insulator")
$call   LockWikiPage("Conductor") // only Basic Conductor is available in first chapter 
$call   LockWikiPage("Insulator") // only Basic Insulator is available in first chapter 


::FirstContractAcceptCh1
@trigger    OnOverarchingLoaded
@cutscene
@once

$call   ReleaseAllHighlights()
{@PAL}      As a trainee, you'll learn to operate four systems...
{@PAL}      ...all recently upgraded aboard this obsolete ship.
{@Player}   Hey! She's got plenty of life left in her!
{@PAL}      Start with either the Research  or Chip Design. 


//written to stablish PAL is sure about something that he is later incorrect about - AI literacy thread.
//TODO - this breaks the game if you do research after design because the game is calling this and before supply chain at the same time. 
::AfterResearchCh1
@trigger    OnOverarchingLoaded
@when       IsSolutionFoundFor(Research)
@cutscene
@once
{@PAL}      Research complete! Conductor and insulator verified.
{@Player}   You're sure?
{@PAL}      Absolutely, Captain.

//SUGGESTION - KACY 
// If we do add this dialogue above in, maybe adding a few more lines to establish PAL and Locke's relationship further - Sarah: i think the comic has done a lot of this. 


:: BeforeSupplyChainCh1
@trigger    OnOverarchingLoaded
@when       IsSolutionFoundFor(Design), IsSolutionFoundFor(Research)
@cutscene
@once
{@PAL}      You'll need materials before you start fabricating the microchips. 


{@Player}	I'll call the Hauler company. 
//phone dial 
{@Quinn}    Oh... Locke! Hiya! Suprised to see your face, is Dorian sick? 
{@Player}	It's a long story -- I'll tell you later. 
//Sarah: I am going to have Quinn give him the nickname "cowboy" to thread the idea of the space western. :)
{@Quinn}    Okay, <i>Cowboy.</i> Going off on your own, eh?
{@Quinn}    Sounds fun. You can count on me to wrangle the haulers for you.

//Sarah: kacy we can't add so many lines. I like these lines, but if we are going to bring in personality, we have to do it within the current line counts I have without losing content. Some of this has to remain more flat at the start of the game because so much onboarding is happening here. 
//{@Quinn}    Ooo, the drama, the suspense, the mystique! Please do tell more.  
//@{Player}	I'm planning the routes now, well, I'm running everthing. It's a long story -- I'll tell you later. 
//{@Quinn}    Okay, Cap'. I’ve got you. But I'm holding you to it.
//{@Quinn}    You decide where you want to get your materials. I’ll handle the haulers.
//{@Player}   Sounds easy enough. Talk to you later.

